Edge Services API

USAGE:
  scw edge-services <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  backend-stage Backend-stage management commands
  cache-stage   Cache-stage management commands
  dns-stage     DNS-stage management commands
  pipeline      Pipeline management commands
  plan          Plan management commands
  purge-request Purge-request management commands
  route-rules   Route-rules management commands
  route-stage   Route-stage management commands
  tls-stage     TLS-stage management commands
  waf-stage     WAF-stage management commands

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for edge-services
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw edge-services [command] --help" for more information about a command.
